WEBVTT

00:00:00.723 --> 00:00:02.773
Verb tense and verb forms.

00:00:02.773 --> 00:00:06.971
Match the time clues, and make sure every sentence has one main verb.

00:00:08.511 --> 00:00:10.161
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:10.161 --> 00:00:13.136
The choices are one verb in different tenses.

00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:17.610
And the passage has time clues, like dates, since, or by the time.

00:00:18.648 --> 00:00:21.225
It's testing whether the verb fits the timeline.

00:00:22.281 --> 00:00:23.556
Here's the method.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:27.991
Hunt for time clues: dates, words like since, and the other verbs.

00:00:27.991 --> 00:00:33.921
Pick the time frame: finished in the past, past up to now, or an even earlier past.

00:00:33.921 --> 00:00:36.846
Check the sentence has one real main verb.

00:00:36.846 --> 00:00:39.843
And keep lists in the same tense all the way through.

00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:44.581
Rule one: a finished past date takes the simple past.

00:00:44.581 --> 00:00:47.706
In nineteen twenty-eight, Fleming has noticed is wrong.

00:00:47.706 --> 00:00:48.893
Fleming noticed.

00:00:49.973 --> 00:00:52.923
Rule two: since means has or have.

00:00:52.923 --> 00:00:55.113
Since nineteen forty-five, the U.

00:00:55.113 --> 00:00:55.803
N.

00:00:55.803 --> 00:00:57.378
expanded is wrong.

00:00:57.378 --> 00:00:59.547
It has expanded, from then up to now.

00:01:00.606 --> 00:01:04.131
Rule three: for an even earlier past, use had.

00:01:04.131 --> 00:01:07.855
By fifteen nineteen, the Aztecs had already built a huge city.

00:01:08.914 --> 00:01:10.134
Let's try one.

00:01:10.134 --> 00:01:11.809
Hunt for time clues.

00:01:11.809 --> 00:01:13.284
Eighteen twenty-five.

00:01:13.284 --> 00:01:14.409
By the time.

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:16.339
And took, in the past tense.

00:01:16.339 --> 00:01:17.984
This is all in the past.

00:01:17.984 --> 00:01:19.459
Completes is present.

00:01:19.459 --> 00:01:21.234
Will complete is future.

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:25.059
And has completed connects to now, not to the eighteen twenties.

00:01:25.059 --> 00:01:28.334
Had completed means finished by a point in the past.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:29.695
The answer is C.

00:01:30.773 --> 00:01:32.698
Watch out for has versus had.

00:01:32.698 --> 00:01:34.173
Has connects to now.

00:01:34.173 --> 00:01:36.477
Had points to an even earlier past.

00:01:37.511 --> 00:01:39.366
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:39.366 --> 00:01:40.421
How to spot it.

00:01:40.421 --> 00:01:41.796
The four steps.

00:01:41.796 --> 00:01:43.216
The tense rules.

00:01:43.216 --> 00:01:44.266
And the trap.

00:01:44.266 --> 00:01:47.001
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
